<h2 id="Introduction">Introduction<a class="anchor-link" href="#Introduction">¶</a></h2><p>In the modern financial industry, loan default prediction is one of the most critical challenges faced by banks and lending institutions. As financial institutions extend credit to individuals and businesses, the risk of loan defaults can significantly impact their profitability and stability. To mitigate these risks and ensure a robust loan approval process, institutions rely on data-driven machine learning models that can identify key factors influencing loan repayment behavior.</p>
<p>In previous assignments, we explored and built a Decision Tree Classifier to predict loan defaults using historical data. The Decision Tree model provided valuable insights by visualizing decision rules and capturing complex relationships in the dataset. However, Decision Trees are prone to overfitting, and their performance can be sensitive to small changes in the data. To enhance our understanding of predictive modeling and improve generalizability, this assignment introduces Logistic Regression, a fundamental yet powerful classification algorithm.</p>
