<h2 id="Why-Logistic-Regression?">Why Logistic Regression?<a class="anchor-link" href="#Why-Logistic-Regression?">¶</a></h2><p>Logistic Regression is widely used in the financial industry due to its simplicity, interpretability, and efficiency in handling binary classification tasks. Unlike linear regression, which predicts continuous values, logistic regression applies a sigmoid function to constrain outputs between 0 and 1, making it suitable for probability-based classifications.</p>
<p>This assignment will focus on building a Logistic Regression Model to predict loan defaults and comparing its performance with the previously implemented Decision Tree model. By doing so, we will determine whether logistic regression provides better accuracy, generalization, and interpretability in identifying high-risk loan applicants.</p>
