</div>
<div class="jp-InputArea jp-Cell-inputArea"><div class="jp-InputPrompt jp-InputArea-prompt">
</div><div class="jp-RenderedHTMLCommon jp-RenderedMarkdown jp-MarkdownOutput" data-mime-type="text/markdown">
<p>Feature scaling is an essential step in data preprocessing that ensures all numerical features are on the same scale, preventing certain features from dominating others due to differing ranges. Standardization is a common method that transforms numerical features to have a mean of 0 and a standard deviation of 1.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="jp-Cell jp-MarkdownCell jp-Notebook-cell" id="cell-id=b3d2171a-b0cd-4885-a034-831fe98b0011">
<div class="jp-Cell-inputWrapper" tabindex="0">
<div class="jp-Collapser jp-InputCollapser jp-Cell-inputCollapser">
</div>
<div class="jp-InputArea jp-Cell-inputArea"><div class="jp-InputPrompt jp-InputArea-prompt">
</div><div class="jp-RenderedHTMLCommon jp-RenderedMarkdown jp-MarkdownOutput" data-mime-type="text/markdown">
<p><strong>Why Standardization?</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>It improves model performance, especially for algorithms that rely on distance calculations, such as Logistic Regression.</li>
<li>It accelerates convergence during optimization.</li>
<li>It prevents large-magnitude features from disproportionately influencing the model.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Code:</strong></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div><div class="jp-Cell jp-CodeCell jp-Notebook-cell jp-mod-noOutputs" id="cell-id=9d815c98-0f9a-413c-9b35-2d42e78478d0">
