<h4 id="3.3-Log-Odds-and-Odds-Ratios-in-Logistic-Regression"><strong>3.3 Log-Odds and Odds Ratios in Logistic Regression</strong><a class="anchor-link" href="#3.3-Log-Odds-and-Odds-Ratios-in-Logistic-Regression">¶</a></h4><p><strong>A. Log-Odds Transformation</strong></p>
<p>Logistic regression models the probability of the positive class ( P(y=1) ) using the sigmoid function. We can rewrite it in terms of odds:</p>
<pre><code>                         Odds= P(y=1)/1−P(y=1)

</code></pre>
<p>​
Taking the logarithm of both sides gives us the log-odds:</p>
<pre><code>                log(P(y=1)/1−P(y=1)) = β0+β1x1+β2x2+...+βnxn
</code></pre>
<p>​
This equation forms the basis of logistic regression.</p>
<ul>
<li>If β 1 is positive, increasing 𝑥1 increases the odds of y=1.</li>
<li>If β 1 is negative, increasing 𝑥1 decreases the odds of y=1.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="jp-Cell jp-MarkdownCell jp-Notebook-cell" id="cell-id=a519456c-1f89-4395-80e8-6e8d9bc1c40d">
<div class="jp-Cell-inputWrapper" tabindex="0">
<div class="jp-Collapser jp-InputCollapser jp-Cell-inputCollapser">
</div>
<div class="jp-InputArea jp-Cell-inputArea"><div class="jp-InputPrompt jp-InputArea-prompt">
</div><div class="jp-RenderedHTMLCommon jp-RenderedMarkdown jp-MarkdownOutput" data-mime-type="text/markdown">
<p><strong>B. Interpreting the Odds Ratio</strong></p>
<p>The odds ratio (OR) is obtained by exponentiating the logistic regression coefficients:</p>
<pre><code>                 OR𝑗 = 𝑒𝛽𝑗 

</code></pre>
<ul>
<li>If OR𝑗&gt;1 an increase in 𝑥𝑗 increases the odds of y=1.</li>
<li>If OR𝑗&lt;1 an increase in 𝑥𝑗 decreases the odds of y=1.</li>
<li>If OR𝑗=1, 𝑥𝑗 has no effect on the probability of y=1.</li>
</ul>
<p>Example Interpretation:</p>
<p>If 𝛽1=0.7, then:</p>
<pre><code>            OR1 = 𝑒^0.7 ≈ 2.01

</code></pre>
<p>This means that for each 1-unit increase in 𝑥1, the odds of y=1 increase by a factor of 2.01.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
