<h4 id="4.1-Train-the-Logistic-Regression-Model"><strong>4.1 Train the Logistic Regression Model</strong><a class="anchor-link" href="#4.1-Train-the-Logistic-Regression-Model">¶</a></h4><p>Logistic Regression is a statistical model used for binary classification problems. It predicts the probability of an event occurring using the sigmoid (logistic) function:</p>
<pre><code>                    P(Y=1∣X)= 1/1+e −(β0+β1X1+⋯+βnXn)
</code></pre>
<p>Where:</p>
<ul>
<li>P(Y=1∣X) is the probability that the output belongs to class 1.</li>
<li>β0 is the intercept (bias term).</li>
<li>𝛽1,𝛽2,...,𝛽𝑛 are the coefficients (weights) of the features.</li>
<li>𝑋1,𝑋2,...,𝑋𝑛are the input features.</li>
</ul>
<p>Logistic Regression is trained using Maximum Likelihood Estimation (MLE) to find the best parameters that maximize the probability of correctly classifying the observations.</p>
</div>
