<h2 id="What-if-?-:-Model-Predicts-Only-One-Class">What if ? : Model Predicts Only One Class<a class="anchor-link" href="#What-if-?-:-Model-Predicts-Only-One-Class">¶</a></h2><p>If our logistic regression model predict only one class (Non-Default: 0) and completely ignoring the Default class (1). Then we will get:</p>
<ul>
<li>Precision, Recall, and F1-score for Class 1 will be 0.00</li>
<li>Confusion Matrix will shows 0 true positives and false negatives for class 1</li>
<li>Model Accuracy (91.92%) will be misleading due to class imbalance.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="jp-Cell jp-MarkdownCell jp-Notebook-cell" id="cell-id=b346da99-1e47-400d-801b-19825837be1d">
<div class="jp-Cell-inputWrapper" tabindex="0">
<div class="jp-Collapser jp-InputCollapser jp-Cell-inputCollapser">
</div>
<div class="jp-InputArea jp-Cell-inputArea"><div class="jp-InputPrompt jp-InputArea-prompt">
</div><div class="jp-RenderedHTMLCommon jp-RenderedMarkdown jp-MarkdownOutput" data-mime-type="text/markdown">
<h2 id="Solution:-Handle-Class-Imbalance">Solution: Handle Class Imbalance<a class="anchor-link" href="#Solution:-Handle-Class-Imbalance">¶</a></h2><p>Since the dataset will be highly imbalanced (many more non-defaulters than defaulters), logistic regression tends to favor the majority class. We can fix it using:</p>
<ol>
<li>Class Weight Adjustment (class_weight='balanced')</li>
<li>SMOTE (Synthetic Minority Oversampling)</li>
<li>Threshold Tuning (Adjusting Decision Boundary) <strong>or</strong> Manually Set class_weight Instead of balanced</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="jp-Cell jp-MarkdownCell jp-Notebook-cell" id="cell-id=6f0d81da-e671-43a4-a008-2072fd554ca6">
<div class="jp-Cell-inputWrapper" tabindex="0">
<div class="jp-Collapser jp-InputCollapser jp-Cell-inputCollapser">
</div>
<div class="jp-InputArea jp-Cell-inputArea"><div class="jp-InputPrompt jp-InputArea-prompt">
</div><div class="jp-RenderedHTMLCommon jp-RenderedMarkdown jp-MarkdownOutput" data-mime-type="text/markdown">
<h4 id="Procedure---1:-Use-Class-Weight-Balancing"><strong>Procedure - 1: Use Class Weight Balancing</strong><a class="anchor-link" href="#Procedure---1:-Use-Class-Weight-Balancing">¶</a></h4><p>Modify our logistic regression to balance class weights:</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div><div class="jp-Cell jp-CodeCell jp-Notebook-cell" id="cell-id=601ce0b1-8c0a-4f59-b5eb-8bc157bb90d5">
<div class="jp-Cell-inputWrapper" tabindex="0">
<div class="jp-Collapser jp-InputCollapser jp-Cell-inputCollapser">
</div>
<div class="jp-InputArea jp-Cell-inputArea">
<div class="jp-InputPrompt jp-InputArea-prompt">In [2584]:</div>
<div class="jp-CodeMirrorEditor jp-Editor jp-InputArea-editor" data-type="inline">
<div class="cm-editor cm-s-jupyter">
<div class="highlight hl-ipython3"><pre><span></span><span class="c1"># Train logistic regression with balanced class weights</span>
<span class="n">model_balanced</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">LogisticRegression</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">class_weight</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s1">'balanced'</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">random_state</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">42</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">max_iter</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">500</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="n">model_balanced</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">fit</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">X_train</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">y_train</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="c1"># Predicting again</span>
<span class="n">y_pred_balanced</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">model_balanced</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">predict</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">X_test</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="c1"># Evaluating performance</span>
<span class="n">accuracy</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">accuracy_score</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">y_test</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">y_pred_balanced</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="nb">print</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="sa">f</span><span class="s1">'Balanced Model Accuracy: </span><span class="si">{</span><span class="n">accuracy</span><span class="si">:</span><span class="s1">.4f</span><span class="si">}</span><span class="s1">'</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="c1"># Confusion Matrix</span>
<span class="nb">print</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s1">'Confusion Matrix:'</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="nb">print</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">confusion_matrix</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">y_test</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">y_pred_balanced</span><span class="p">))</span>

<span class="c1"># Classification Report</span>
<span class="nb">print</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s1">'Classification Report:'</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="nb">print</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">classification_report</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">y_test</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">y_pred_balanced</span><span class="p">))</span>
</pre></div>
