<h4 id="4.2-Extract-and-Analyze-Model-Coefficients"><strong>4.2 Extract and Analyze Model Coefficients</strong><a class="anchor-link" href="#4.2-Extract-and-Analyze-Model-Coefficients">¶</a></h4><p>The coefficients (β) in Logistic Regression indicate the importance of each feature:</p>
<ul>
<li>Positive Coefficient: The feature increases the likelihood of loan default.</li>
<li>Negative Coefficient: The feature decreases the likelihood of loan default.</li>
<li>Magnitude: Larger absolute values indicate stronger impact.</li>
</ul>
<p>Since the coefficients are in log-odds space, we can exponentiate them to interpret their effect as odds ratios:</p>
<pre><code>        Odds Ratio = eβ

</code></pre>
<ul>
<li>Odds Ratio &gt; 1: The feature increases the probability of default.</li>
<li>Odds Ratio &lt; 1: The feature decreases the probability of default.</li>
<li>Odds Ratio = 1: The feature has no effect.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
