<h2 id="Final-Verdict:-Which-Model-to-Use?">Final Verdict: Which Model to Use?<a class="anchor-link" href="#Final-Verdict:-Which-Model-to-Use?">¶</a></h2><p><strong>Best for Accuracy → Logistic Regression (92%)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Logistic Regression performs better in overall accuracy but fails to detect defaults due to extreme class imbalance.</li>
<li>Suitable for use cases where avoiding false positives is more critical than catching all defaulters.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Best for Default Detection (Higher Recall) → Decision Tree</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>The Decision Tree captures more defaulters than logistic regression.</li>
<li>However, it suffers from overfitting and lower overall accuracy.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Best Strategy? Use a Hybrid Approach</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Use Logistic Regression for overall classification and interpretability.</li>
<li>Combine with Decision Tree to improve recall for defaulters.</li>
<li>Apply Class Balancing (SMOTE or Class Weights) to improve the recall of defaulters.</li>
<li>Consider Ensemble Models like Random Forest or XGBoost for improved performance.</li>
</ul>
